# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RE-SUPPLY, 4 September 2026. Two Envision budgetary commercial offers were supplied again.
#
# They carry the SAME VERSION AND DATE as the two recorded above — both still "Version: 01",
# both still "Date of Submission: August 31, 2026" — but they are NOT the same documents. The
# text was compared against the 3 September copies held in the private repository and DIFFERS
# SUBSTANTIVELY. These are SILENT REVISIONS: the content changed and the version and date did not.
#
#   1. The 10 MW offer's BESS warranty was CUT from 5 years to 2 years upon Substantial
#      Completion. The 11 MW offer's stayed at 5 years. The 10 MW document is now internally
#      inconsistent as a result: its executive summary still promises "5 years' BESS Warranty",
#      which the edit did not reach.
#   2. The scope note "PCS and AC equipment are not included in supply scope" was REMOVED from
#      BOTH offers. In the 3 September copies that exclusion contradicted the offers' own price
#      tables, which charge separately for "PCS & MV Transformers". Deleting it resolves that
#      contradiction in the buyer's favour.
#
# Both headline prices are unchanged in both offers. So on the 10 MW offer the price held while
# the warranty was reduced.
#
# This repeats a pattern already on the record for this OEM: the 5 August design calculation
# silently revised the 29 July one while both were labelled V1.0.
#
# The 4 September copies do NOT supersede the 3 September copies automatically — which issue
# governs is a question for the bidder, and both are recorded here so the divergence cannot be
# lost.
#
# The documents themselves are held on the same basis as the rest of this manifest: private
# repository, recorded here by hash. The terms recited above, and clause 6 quoted below, ARE
# disclosed in this public repository — see the header note. Clause 6 reads, verbatim:
#
#   "The offer is confidential thus shall be used by the Employer/EPC exclusively for the
#    evaluation of the project, and may not be broadcasted, published, or, more generally,
#    communicated to any third party without prior, explicit and written authorization from
#    Envision."
#
# This repository is public, so the recitation above falls within the "published" case that
# clause names, and no authorization instrument is held. That is recorded plainly here rather
# than left implicit. Offer validity is 30 days from 31 August 2026, so both offers lapse on
# 30 September 2026.
#
